# Chameleon UI — AI consumer rules

When generating or editing a **consumer** app (including stock-analyzer) that uses `@chameleon-ui/*`:

1. Obey [`chameleon-ui/AGENTS.md`](chameleon-ui/AGENTS.md). Longer attach notes: [`docs/ai/agent-consume.md`](docs/ai/agent-consume.md).
2. Call MCP `get_import_specifiers` before writing imports. Preferred CSS is `@chameleon-ui/themes/cupertino/css`, **not** `@chameleon-ui/themes/cupertino/variables.css`.
3. Never write `workspace:*` into a non-pnpm-workspace `package.json`. Link all five packages of the chosen graph (React or Vue; see AGENTS.md). Vue: `@chameleon-ui/components-vue` (catalog 103/103 + ThemeProvider).
4. `get_contract` by slug before emitting a component. `get_design_rules` before theme density/RTL.
5. SchemaRenderer default map is 10 slugs. `adapter-ag-ui` is POC. Do not invent `generation_quality` scores.
